{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536282-fetishes-of-protection","id":1536282,"title":"Fetishes of protection","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-25T17:39:48-07:00","id":1536282,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Fetishes of protection","content":"Hey everybody! I\u2019m playing in a pbp game on discord and my character a BG Homid Ahroun, is one I created to be more of a protector type of character. Stick up for the little guy and rage against the bully is the idea I had in mind. So one of the ideas I was kicking around was a fetish shield. But in my search for pre made fetishes I came up pretty dry. So I come to the internet not just for inspiration for a shield but also protection fetishes in general. With the resources I have fetishes of protection seem to be lacking (which kinda makes sense) but it\u2019d be nice to amend that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28463-bwhite24","name":"Bwhite24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T23:31:25-07:00","id":1536284,"title":"","content":"The second Werewolf Players Guide has a level 2 fetish Bones of Shielding which provides extra soak dice based on one's Gnosis score.<br /> <br /> There are other fetishes that could be construed as &quot;protective&quot;, but not directly provide defense against damage. Whether they count as protective really depends on what you consider to be protection. Does a fetish that warns you of the presence of the Wyrm be considered protective? What about a fetish that prevents you from drowning? Or a fetish that reveals the location and condition of a specific kinfolk? What about a fetish that warns you of danger? Or prevents botches? There are published fetishes that do all of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T04:52:49-07:00","id":1536339,"title":"","content":"I got few idea for protective kind of fetiche, something that prevent your mind from being influenced by external powers (mind control, Domination discipline...), that give you additionnal dice for defense roll (dodging, blocking...), allow you to sense your near environement to detect any ennemy including coming from behind (preventing them from a -2 and -1 difficulty for attack from side or behind), increase rage roll difficulty to avoid frenezy (usefull for Arhoun with more Rage than Gnosis), something that protect you from wyrm corruption and/or supernatural deseases and poisons and so on<br /> <br /> Problem is how to make it work with only a Gnosis roll or spending one? It would have to be a fixed effect like +3 dice for dodging, or +2 difficulty for mind controlling you, that kind of things. The ST has last word on it.<br /> <br /> In W5 and despite all the things i personnaly don't like in it the fetiche work simply by allowing you an extra power working exactly like gifts, as long as you posess the item (if i read correctly and understood it) you don't have to activate it with Gnosis may it be through a roll or spending a point.<br /> For exemple Apeskin work for as long as you wear it in Homid or Glabro and lose regenerative power but also your vulnerability to silver while the Harmony flute ask a roll with Attribute + Capacity to use it's power.<br /> I'm giving this information because I think it gives the storyteller and the player more freedom to create new fetiches than the exclusive Gnosis, which would be used instead to attuned to them to use their power when the pc obtain them and ask for their help for the first time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}